@startuml AI_SWUpdate_Diagnostic_Flow
skinparam SequenceMessageAlignment center
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 10

title End-to-End SWUpdate AI Diagnostic Architecture (Server-Driven Request Flow)

box "Android ECU Target" #LightGreen
participant "FcSwUpdateSrv\n(SWUpdate Daemon)" as SWU
participant "Android Logcat / OS\n(Process Streams)" as LOGS
participant "ai_service_client\n(Binder Client & Log Collector)" as CLIENT
end box

box "Linux Host / Docker Server (Air-Gapped)" #LightCyan
participant "ai_diagnostic_server\n(Python TCP Server)" as AISERVER
participant "Ollama SLM\n(gemma3:12b)" as SLM
participant "Linux File System\n(/tmp/ai-swupdate-reports/)" as FS
end box

== 1. Initialization & Session Monitoring ==

CLIENT -> SWU : Binder connect & register BnUpdateCallback
activate CLIENT
SWU --> CLIENT : Connection confirmed
CLIENT -> AISERVER : Open Bidirectional TCP Socket (Port 9000)
activate AISERVER

loop SWUpdate Execution Lifecycle
    SWU -> CLIENT : onUpdateState(trUpdState)
    CLIENT -> AISERVER : JSON {"event": "onUpdateState", "state": 5, ...}
    AISERVER -> AISERVER : Record event in session_events

    SWU -> CLIENT : onUpdateProgress(trUpdProgress)
    CLIENT -> AISERVER : JSON {"event": "onUpdateProgress", "module": "system_a", ...}
    AISERVER -> AISERVER : Track progress history
end

== 2. Error Notification & Server-Driven Log Request ==

SWU -> CLIENT : onUpdateError(trErrorIds)
CLIENT -> AISERVER : JSON {"event": "onUpdateError", "errorCode": 28, ...}
AISERVER -> AISERVER : Log critical error event

== 3. API 1: System Details Negotiation ==

AISERVER -> CLIENT : TCP JSON {"command": "request_system_details"}
note over CLIENT
Execute API 1: getSystemInformation()
- product_class: "IVI"
- primary_os: "Android"
- secondary_os: ["Linux"]
end note
CLIENT -> AISERVER : JSON {"event": "systemDetailsResponse", "product_class": "IVI", "primary_os": "Android", ...}

AISERVER -> AISERVER : Compute requested artifacts from SystemDetails\n(e.g., ["update_engine_logs", "logcat_logs", "update_persistent_logs", "downloadpipe"])

== 4. API 2: Dynamic Log Collection & Packaging ==

AISERVER -> CLIENT : TCP JSON {"command": "request_artifacts", "artifacts": ["update_engine_logs", "logcat_logs", ...]}

note over CLIENT
Execute API 2: getRequiredFiles(requestedArtifacts)
1. For each tag: logcat -d -s <TAG> > /data/system/fcswupdate/tmp/ai_diagnostics/<TAG>.log
2. Package all logs into swupdate-diagnostics-<timestamp>.tar.gz
3. Base64 encode archive string
end note

CLIENT -> LOGS : Extract logcat streams for requested tags
activate LOGS
LOGS --> CLIENT : Return log streams
deactivate LOGS

CLIENT -> AISERVER : JSON {"event": "swUpdateDiagnosticArchive", "archiveData": "<base64>", ...}
deactivate CLIENT

== 5. Offline SLM Diagnosis & Report Generation ==

note over AISERVER
1. Save .tar.gz archive to /tmp/ai-swupdate-diagnostics/
2. Extract in-memory log excerpts for analysis
end note

AISERVER -> AISERVER : Assemble diagnostic prompt\n(Error Code + Progress History + Process Logs)

AISERVER -> SLM : HTTP POST /api/generate {"model": "gemma3:12b", "prompt": "..."}
activate SLM
note over SLM
100% Offline Inference
(Air-Gapped Network internal: true)
end note
SLM --> AISERVER : Structured Diagnostic Analysis
deactivate SLM

AISERVER -> FS : Save report file swupdate-report-<timestamp>.md
activate FS
FS --> AISERVER : File saved
deactivate FS

AISERVER -> AISERVER : Print formatted diagnosis report to Terminal / stdout

deactivate AISERVER

@enduml
